---
// "For Clients / For Businesses" audience toggle, matching the
// approved Stitch header's distinction between the two real Chakusa
// audiences (directive sections 4, 10). Real destinations only: no
// separate customer-facing marketplace web page exists yet (the real
// marketplace lives in the mobile app), so "For clients" points at the
// closest real customer-facing destination, browsing businesses by
// industry, rather than a fabricated page.
//
// Stitch renders this as a segmented pill with one side visibly
// active (white, elevated), not two plain equal-weight links. We
// approximate "active" from the current path: pages under /industries
// are the client-facing side, everything else defaults to the
// business side (matching Stitch's own default state).
const path = Astro.url.pathname;
const isClientSide = path.startsWith("/industries");
---
<div class="audience-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Choose your experience">
  <a href="/industries" aria-current={isClientSide ? "page" : undefined}>For clients</a>
  <a href="/business" aria-current={isClientSide ? undefined : "page"}>For businesses</a>
</div>
